@Vudentz Can you clarify the current behavior here now? 
Is it that -EAGAIN is returned before calling `bt_conn_send_cb` and therefore the buf needs to be unref`ed?
In that case I think there is also EMSGSIZE.

Thank you.
Me question about EMSGSIZE still remains then. I think in the case where `bt_l2cap_chan_send` submits the work, and  `l2cap_chan_tx_process` calls `l2cap_chan_le_send_sdu` and returns -EMSGSIZE the buffer seems to be not released, because the application would not receive this error code. It appears to me that the application has acquired the first ref but it is unclear who has the responsebility to release it.
This check here:
```
 	if (total_len > ch->tx.mtu) {
		return -EMSGSIZE;
	}
```
Maybe this check could be moved out of `l2cap_chan_le_send_sdu` in that case?

I'm looking at avdtp BTW, and it appears to not release the buf in case of errors returned. I think we need to document in the API of `bt_l2cap_chan_send` how error handling and buffer releasing should be handled.
